        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-106654",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $y>30$ and $t>0,$ which of the following is an inhibited decay equation?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "An inhibited decay equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-k(y-a),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $y>a$ for all $t>0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited decay equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=840-28y.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-28(y-30).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=28,$ and $a=30.$ Note that for inhibited decay, we must have $y>30$ for all $t>0.$"
      }
    ],
    ":knowledge-point/title": "Identifying Inhibited Decay Equations and Initial Value Problems"
  }
}
